Diagram:
  name: Change Scale Functionality
  version: 1.0
  version-ptd: 1.1
  description: Example of PT (plain text) diagram notation for scale change logic, showing the integration of global settings, scale types, and chord mappings
  files: change-scale.js, globals.js, jam-mapping-to-allowed.js, note-tools.js, chord-to-scale.js, scaleToNotes.js

Imports:
  change-scale.js (function changeScaleFilter, function setActiveScaleFilter, function setActiveScaleFilterToMatchChord)
    --> globals.js (globals)
    --> jam-mapping-to-allowed.js (function buildNoteMap)
    --> note-tools.js (function createChordSymbol)
    --> chord-to-scale.js (function chordSymbolToScaleNames)
    --> scaleToNotes.js (function scaleObjToNotes, function chordNotesToScaleNotes)

Files:
  file: change-scale.js
    Variables:
      const uniq: function
      const Tonal: object
      const globals: object
    Functions:
      changeScaleFilter(scaleFilter: string)
      setActiveScaleFilter(scaleTonic: string, scaleType: string, scaleNotes: array, scaleTypes: array)
      setActiveScaleFilterToMatchChord(chordTonic: string, chordType: string, strategy: string)
      _setActiveScaleFilter(scaleNotes: array) (private)
      clearActiveScaleFilter() (private)
      calcScaleTypesDropdown(chordConfig: object) (private)
    Classes:
      none

  file: globals.js
    Variables:
      (globals is an object)
    Functions:
      none
    Classes:
      none

  file: jam-mapping-to-allowed.js
    Variables:
      (none)
    Functions:
      buildNoteMap(scaleNotes: array, maxChordConfigs: number, lhTriggerOctave: string, rhJamSoundOctave: string, options: object)
    Classes:
      none

  file: note-tools.js
    Variables:
      (none)
    Functions:
      createChordSymbol(chordTonic: string, chordType: string)
    Classes:
      none

  file: chord-to-scale.js
    Variables:
      (none)
    Functions:
      chordSymbolToScaleNames(chordSymbol: string)
    Classes:
      none

  file: scaleToNotes.js
    Variables:
      (none)
    Functions:
      scaleObjToNotes(scaleObj: object)
      chordNotesToScaleNotes(chordNotes: object, scaleNotes: object)
    Classes:
      none

Classes:
  class: (none)

Use Cases:
  Sequence: Change Scale Filtering
    🧑‍💻 -> changeScaleFilter() [change-scale.js]
         checks current scale filter
         -> setActiveScaleFilter() [change-scale.js]
             sets active scale filter
             -> _setActiveScaleFilter() [change-scale.js]
                 updates scale trigger map
                 < void
             < void
         -> reportScaleChange() [change-scale.js]
             broadcasts scale change
             < void
         < void

  Sequence: Set Active Scale Filter
    🧑‍💻 -> setActiveScaleFilter() [change-scale.js]
         sets the active scale filter
         -> globals.scaleFiltering.scaleTonic = scaleObj.tonic [globals.js]
             updates scale tonic
         -> globals.scaleFiltering.scaleType = scaleObj.type [globals.js]
             updates scale type
         -> _setActiveScaleFilter() [change-scale.js]
             updates scale trigger map
             < void
         < void

  Sequence: Playing a Chord
    🧍‍♂️ -> playChord [change-scale.js]
        plays a chord
        -> changeChordTriggerNoteAndThusScale [change-scale.js]
            updates globals.currentChordTriggerNote
            -> changeScaleFilter [change-scale.js]
                determines appropriate scale filter
                [if] scaleName == 'notes of chord'
                    -> _setActiveScaleFilter [change-scale.js]
                [else]
                    normal Tonal scale
                    -> calcScaleTypesDropdown [change-scale.js]
                    -> setActiveScaleFilter [change-scale.js]
                        updates globals.scaleFiltering
                        -> _setActiveScaleFilter [change-scale.js]
                            builds scale trigger map
                        -> reportScaleChange [change-scale.js]
                            broadcasts 'scale-changed' and 'scale-filtering-changed'
                < void
        -> GM [change-scale.js]
            plays notes in GM
        -> Document [change-scale.js]
            broadcasts 'chord-changed' for UI piano roll
    < void
